            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0150" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/445</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-31T20:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                                1918, 8 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 2, 1919, 12.52
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>385. [For] War Trade Board, 71:</p>
                <p>Referring your unnumbered December 29, 3 p.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d124-f1"/>
                    Russian bank notes were not removed from transport <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sheridan</hi>. Transport sailed to-day for Manila. News of the expected
                    arrival of bank notes had been widely spread over Siberia and refusal to permit
                    delivery of same to Russian authorities has created very unfavorable impression
                    toward American work.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
